# Test: enum-refusal-union
#
# QUESTION: does the config parser refuse a value that no member of a union
# accepts, where one member is an enumeration, with the enum refusal: the
# enumeration's values with help in member order, then the other member types
# named in words, a close match when one is close, and the fix? A unit test
# holds a test union; this drives the shipped union through the real
# `ze config validate` entry point, hierarchical and set format.
#
# Leaf: bgp peer <name> connection local ip, `type union { type zt:ip-address;
#   type enumeration { enum auto } }`
#   (internal/component/bgp/yang/ze-bgp-conf.yang, container local).
#
# Producers: validateUnionValue (internal/component/config/schema.go), the
# union arm of refusalFacts.why ("accepts one of these values:" then "or a
# value of type ...", internal/component/config/yang/refusal.go),
# unionMembersFromType (internal/component/config/yang_schema.go).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-config-enum-refusal-proposes-valid-values AC-13 (parser and
#   set-format cases), with the accepted control.
# PREVENTS: `matches no member type`, `or one of`, `invalid enum`, or a union
#   refusal that lists no accepted value.

stdin=autoo:terminator=EOF_AUTOO
bgp {
	router-id 203.0.113.253
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 192.0.2.1
			}
			local {
				ip autoo
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_AUTOO

stdin=far:terminator=EOF_FAR
bgp {
	router-id 203.0.113.253
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 192.0.2.1
			}
			local {
				ip zzzzzz
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_FAR

stdin=setform:terminator=EOF_SETFORM
set bgp router-id 203.0.113.253
set bgp peer peer1 connection remote ip 192.0.2.1
set bgp peer peer1 connection local ip autoo
EOF_SETFORM

stdin=accepted:terminator=EOF_ACCEPTED
bgp {
	router-id 203.0.113.253
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 192.0.2.1
			}
			local {
				ip auto
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_ACCEPTED

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=autoo
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 9: bgp peer peer1 connection local ip: "autoo" is not an accepted value (did you mean auto?)
expect=stdout:pattern=ip accepts one of these values:\n +auto  Let the operating system choose the source address of the connection\.\n *or a value of type ip-address\n *fix: ip auto;
reject=stdout:contains=matches no member type
reject=stdout:contains=or one of
reject=stdout:contains=invalid enum

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=far
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 9: bgp peer peer1 connection local ip: "zzzzzz" is not an accepted value
expect=stdout:contains=or a value of type ip-address
expect=stdout:contains=fix: ip <auto|ip-address>;
reject=stdout:contains=did you mean
reject=stdout:contains=matches no member type

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=setform
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=line 3: bgp peer peer1 connection local ip: "autoo" is not an accepted value (did you mean auto?)
expect=stdout:contains=fix: set bgp peer peer1 connection local ip auto
reject=stdout:contains=matches no member type
reject=stdout:contains=invalid value for

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=accepted
expect=exit:code=0
